## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: ac494c6c2710a207f51a219e3b09360a9c94203c

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I ran `git blame` on the exact buggy line (`tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(... ) + link ;`) at the parent of the fix commit (`0d21114...~1`), which pointed to commit `ac494c6c2710` ("more diagnostics for EA-68014", 2015-05-26).

**(2) Specific change that introduced the bug:** That commit refactored:
```java
if (message.startsWith("<html>")) {
  tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message) + link);
}
else {
  tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message) + link);
}
```
into a single ternary line, but in doing so moved the `+ link` term outside the `wrapInHtml(...)` call:
```java
tooltip = XmlStringUtil.wrapInHtml(message.startsWith("<html>") ? XmlStringUtil.stripHtml(message): XmlStringUtil.escapeString(message)) + link ;
```
This changes the semantics: previously `link` was included inside the `<html>...</html>` wrapper; after the "refactor" it's appended after the closing `</html>` tag, producing malformed tooltip HTML.

**(3) Evidence:** The bug-fixing commit `0d21114` simply moves the closing parenthesis back so `link` is inside `wrapInHtml(...)` again — the exact inverse of what `ac494c6c2710` did. `git blame` on the pre-fix line attributes it directly to `ac494c6c2710`, and the diff of that commit shows the operator-precedence/parenthesization mistake introduced alongside an unrelated large refactor (getFile() indirection, ProblemsHolder annotations, etc.) for diagnostic purposes — the tooltip logic change appears to be an unintended side effect of that refactor rather than its main purpose, consistent with a "not all warnings displayed" bug caused by broken tooltip HTML.

I'm confident in this attribution — the blame result directly matches the line touched by the fix, and the diff shows a clear, isolated logic regression at that commit.

